    <comp lib="7" loc="(325,65)" name="Text">
      <a name="font" val="SansSerif bold 20"/>
      <a name="text" val="Hazard Shield (Decode Stage)"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="7" loc="(50,230)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">By reading an assortment of control and data path values, the Hazard
Shield determines if an instruction in the Execute (E) or Memory Access (M)
stages will overwrite either of the registers read by the instruction in the
Decode (D) stage. In the case that read register data will be overwritten by an
instruction in a later pipeline stage, the Hazard Shield determines--to the
best of its ability--the overwriting value so it can be forwarded to the
Decode (D) stage.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="7" loc="(55,115)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="left"/>
      <a name="text">This circuit enables data forwarding within the Decode (D) stage.  The
Hazard Shield aims to prevent data hazards by checking if an instruction
further in the pipeline will overwrite any of the registers read by the
current instruction. However, users should note that this does not prevent
ALL data hazards.</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="7" loc="(600,680)" name="Text">
      <a name="font" val="SansSerif bold 10"/>
      <a name="text">Cannot forward data from
Execute (E) stage if the
instruction in the Execute (E)
stage loads value from
memory into register
(RegWriteDataSrc == 0b10)</a>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="7" loc="(680,715)" name="Text">
      <a name="text" val="-&gt;"/>
    </comp>
